    "created_at": "2024-02-15T14:21:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-15T14:21:57Z",
    "body": "Yes, no browser [supports it currently](https://jsfiddle.net/v0wq3mnu/), and I believe that at least in Worker scope it's admitted that we'll never have it because that would mean to move the DOM there.  \r\nMight be worth removing it from the specs entirely indeed.  \r\n\r\nFor the ones that really want a bitmap version of an svg Blob, it's still possible through the blob: URL + `<img>` route, even if that's a bit convoluted:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nif (blob.type === \"image/svg+xml\") {\r\n  const img = new Image();\r\n  img.src = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\r\n  await img.decode();\r\n  URL.revokeObjectURL(img.src);\r\n  return createImageBitmap(img);\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
